students at desert oasis high school in  the southwest valley really concerned  for their safety now their parents want  to see some change so all this comes  after a handful of incidents over the  last couple of weeks victoria saha is  live tonight with the message parents  and students want the school district to  hear victoria  two big questions here tonight when will  the violence stop at desert oasis and  when will the school board step in to  help stop that violence one parent  actually hosted her own meeting tonight  helping parents to be vocal about  holding school leaders accountable when  it comes to keeping their children safe  at schools  at this point school doesn't feel like a  safe place that he should a comment  heartbreaking to hear from any student  every time that intercom goes off i  don't know if it's just me or anybody  else it sends me to like a little  anxiety attack this is the constant  worry for students like christian  melhausen a junior at desert oasis  earlier this month there was a gun  reported on campus then the next day a  fight broke out in the common area  prompting the lockdowns then just this  past friday a student was arrested after  a gun was found on campus there has to  be a way so that our kids can go to  school and feel safe which is why parent  sheriff morgan is taking matters into  her own hands she heard from the school  staff but felt they did not help address  the issues at bay and thinks more can be  done basically working with the student  to figure out why they did what they did  and how do we prevent them from doing it  further another parent who wanted to  remain anonymous tells us she  volunteered to be a monitor back in  december at desert oasis she gives us a  summary of what she saw there was no  admin walking around nobody was telling  anybody to go to class except for me  morgan says she has reached out to every  school board member to add school safety  as an agenda item for thursday night's  school board 